# phys2d ignore rules.
#
# Policy: `build/` is disposable local output (PHYSICS_ENGINE_GUIDE.md §2 says receipts
# there are "not guaranteed to exist in a clean clone"). Toolchains, vendored
# dependencies, compiled binaries, generated HTML replays and dev-server logs are never
# committed.
#
# Exception: the small *textual* evidence files that the documentation cites as receipts
# (logs, benchmark CSVs, the energy SVG, exit-status files) ARE committed, because a
# reader following a `build/...` link should find the file instead of a 404. The
# exception is by file type and directory, listed explicitly below.
#
# Exception: the nine browser assets the showcase actually serves are committed under
# build/web/ (README: "The output is nine required files ... Keep them together").

# ---- build output, toolchains, vendored dependencies -------------------------------
/build/**
# directory shells needed before any nested file can be re-included
!/build/browser-check/
!/build/mission-audit/
!/build/prepared/
!/build/temporal/
!/build/web/
# textual receipts cited by the docs (top level of build/)
!/build/*.csv
!/build/*.log
!/build/*.err
!/build/*.svg
# textual receipts inside the documented receipt directories
!/build/browser-check/*.log
!/build/mission-audit/*.log
!/build/mission-audit/*.exit
!/build/prepared/*.csv
!/build/prepared/*.log
!/build/prepared/*.exit
!/build/temporal/*.log
# the nine assets served by the browser showcase (nothing else in build/web/)
!/build/web/index.html
!/build/web/index.js
!/build/web/index.wasm
!/build/web/showcase.css
!/build/web/core.js
!/build/web/scenes.js
!/build/web/render.js
!/build/web/instrument.js
!/build/web/showcase.js

# generated HTML frame replays: reproduce with
#   ./build/demo_broadphase build/<scene>_demo.html <scene>
/build/*.html

# compiled objects and binaries anywhere (safety net)
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb

# ---- local client metadata, editor and OS cruft ------------------------------------
.freebuff/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
